<section id="who" class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Made for the way <span class="highlight">you fly</span></h2>
  <div class="resource-cards">
    <article>
      <h3>A club with a fleet</h3>
      <p>Fifteen aircraft, none equipped, and an installed unit costs hundreds of euros each before the engineer. A few Go on the key shelf cover every aircraft in the air. Each lasts the day on one charge.</p>
      <p><%= link_to_page "blog/club-fleet", label: "How a club shares them" %></p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A pilot who flies other people&rsquo;s aircraft</h3>
      <p>The club&rsquo;s on Saturday, a friend&rsquo;s on Sunday, a rental on holiday, none equipped the same. A Tango in the flight bag shows ADS-L, FLARM and ADS-B on the same radar in every cockpit.</p>
      <p><%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "skyBlip Tango" %></p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A small cockpit with no room left</h3>
      <p>A microlight, a vintage replica or a homebuilt with a full panel and no power socket. Go fits in a hand, runs on its battery and stays readable in full sun.</p>
      <p><%= link_to_page "mount", label: "Mount it in the cockpit" %></p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A field shared with gliders</h3>
      <p>Gliders and tugs carry FLARM. Go shows them on its radar and gives the direction of the one closing in, without a FLARM of your own.</p>
      <p><%= link_to_page "features", label: "skyBlip Go" %></p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>An aircraft with a transponder</h3>
      <p>Air traffic control sees your transponder, but a microlight with only ADS-L or FLARM does not. Go adds ADS-L under your aircraft&rsquo;s own address, and shows you the FLARM traffic too.</p>
      <p><%= link_to_page "blog/who-sees-ads-l", label: "Who sees what" %></p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A SafeSky user far from the network</h3>
      <p>SafeSky goes blind where mobile coverage ends, which is where light aircraft fly. Go works from aircraft to aircraft with no network, beside the app you already use.</p>
      <p><%= link_to_page "blog/network-or-radio", label: "Network or radio" %></p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="signature"><%= link_to_page "compare", label: "Compare with installed and other devices" %></p>
</section>

<section id="where-to-look" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">See and be seen, <span class="highlight">with a Go</span></h2>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3>A radar <span class="highlight">you can read at a glance</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        You are in the centre, track up. Each traffic icon shows whether the aircraft
        is above, level with you or below. Its line shows where it will be in a minute.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "radar.png", alt: "The radar page: three aircraft, one above, one below, one level and climbing, each with a line showing where it will be in a minute" %>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3>An alarm <span class="highlight">that gives the direction</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        Within 3&nbsp;km and 300&nbsp;m, a quarter of the screen flashes on the
        side of the traffic.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "alarm.png", alt: "The radar page during an alarm: the quarter of the screen facing the traffic has turned black" %>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3>Your position <span class="highlight">broadcast every second</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        In flight, the Go broadcasts your position in ADS-L every second. Aircraft
        with ADS-L see you. Your callsign goes in a separate message and
        only appears on equipment that reads it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot">
      <%= screen_image_tag "nearby.png", alt: "The Nearby page: five aircraft, those at your height first, with their source ADS-L or FLARM, their callsign, their distance and their height above or below you" %>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="feature feature--reverse">
    <div>
      <h3>The traffic <span class="highlight">in your app</span>.</h3>
      <p>
        Over Bluetooth, the traffic shows up in SDVFR Next, SkyDemon,
        ForeFlight and other apps.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="shot shot--photo shot--app">
      <%= pages_image_tag "sdvfr-next-traffic.avif", alt: "SDVFR Next: the map with the traffic received from skyBlip Go, each aircraft labelled with its callsign" %>
      <figcaption>SkyDreamSoft SDVFR Next <a href="https://skydreamsoft.fr">skydreamsoft.fr</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <p class="signature"><%= link_to_page "features", label: "See every feature" %></p>
</section>

<section id="simulator" class="band band--tint try-radar">
