<section id="questions" class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">What pilots ask before buying</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Who can see me?</summary>
      <p>Pilots with equipment that can receive your ADS-L signal can see the position your Go transmits. Go receives FLARM but doesn&rsquo;t transmit it. Bravo doesn&rsquo;t transmit your position. Air traffic control radar doesn&rsquo;t show ADS-L: carry the transponder your airspace requires.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why ADS-L and not ADS-B?</summary>
      <p>ADS-L transmits at 25&nbsp;mW, so a pocket device runs a day on its battery, and it needs no certification. ADS-B needs a certified transponder of 70&nbsp;W or more, and portable ADS-B may not transmit in the EU. Bravo still lets you see ADS-B aircraft. <%= link_to_page "blog/why-ads-l", label: "Why ADS-L" %>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>I already use SafeSky. Why add a Go?</summary>
      <p>SafeSky needs mobile coverage. Go works from aircraft to aircraft without it, and makes you visible to every ADS-L receiver around you. The two work side by side. <%= link_to_page "blog/network-or-radio", label: "Network or radio" %>.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I see aircraft with transponders?</summary>
      <p>Yes for aircraft equipped with ADS-B. With Bravo, their positions appear in your navigation app or on a paired Go. Mode S alone gives no position. Bravo detects it, and we&rsquo;re collecting data to work out how best to report it on Go and in navigation apps.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a subscription?</summary>
      <p>No. You buy the hardware. Position transmissions, traffic, alerts and updates need no subscription.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is it certified?</summary>
      <p>No. skyBlip is an uncertified aid to visual lookout. Keep looking outside. Aircraft won&rsquo;t appear unless your device receives a compatible signal. Keep the equipment required for your flight.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a phone?</summary>
      <p>Go has its own screen. With Bravo on its own, use a compatible app on a phone or tablet to see traffic. In a Tango, Go shows it.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I go back to the original software?</summary>
      <p>Yes. skyBlip leaves the program that installs the software in place. You can download the original software of the T-Echo and the X1 from the web to reinstall it.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
  <p class="signature">More answers on the <%= link_to_page "features", label: "Go", anchor: "questions" %>, <%= link_to_page "skyblip-bravo", label: "Bravo", anchor: "questions" %> and <%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "Tango", anchor: "questions" %> pages.</p>
</section>

